# Test files & results
test_results/
test_*.py
# ...but the python-server suite is real, committed, and run by CI
# (`python -m pytest -q .`). The blanket rule above is for ad-hoc scratch
# scripts; without this negation every *new* test file is silently left out of
# the repo and therefore out of CI, which is how test_api_endpoints.py once
# went unrun long enough for one of its tests to pin a bug as the spec.
!python-server/test_*.py
eval_*.py
check_*.py
compare_*.py
create_test_audio.py
extract_stt.py

# Dev build scripts
run-dev.bat
build-llama*.bat
.cargo/

# Test audio
*.wav

# Process artifacts (session specs/plans) stay local-only — public repo carries the product
docs/superpowers/
docs/release-signing/
docs/specs/
